= Energy efficiency — Technical =

== Energy conversion metric ==
For a converter in which both terms are measured as energy over a specified interval:

<pre>
eta = E_useful_out / E_input
</pre>

This dimensionless definition requires a specified service and system boundary. For a physically consistent energy accounting, eta is no greater than one when useful energy is a subset of supplied energy; a heat pump's coefficient of performance is not the same definition.

== Service and system-level metrics ==
Lighting is commonly compared using luminous efficacy (lumens per watt), while a computing service may use useful work per joule. Those performance ratios have different dimensions and do not constitute the same thermodynamic efficiency. Integrated energy systems require all relevant auxiliary loads, duration, losses and energy storage changes to be considered.

== Evidence and limitations ==
A reproducible comparison states the input fuel/electricity basis, measurement interval, operating conditions, measurement uncertainty, useful-service definition and upstream/downstream boundary. Rebound effects affect total usage, not the device conversion ratio by itself.

